In your simulation, this becomes the game mechanic. The "world" is made of interconnected systems that organically grow according to rules. AI agents observe metrics, create branches, provision new components, rebalance workloads, archive stale resources, and restructure infrastructure. Rather than hard-coded progression, the simulation evolves as a consequence of policy decisions and resource constraints.

One extension that fits your vision is a Topology Evolution Engine. Instead of fixed architectures, it continuously evaluates the environment and proposes structural changes:

