Vistamations becomes the orchestration layer rather than the hosting provider.

Distributed Compute

The architecture could look like:

                     ROOT AUTHORITY

                           │

           ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐

           │               │               │

      Local Compute    Cloud Compute    Edge Compute

           │               │               │

        Desktop         Google Cloud     Cloudflare

        Laptop          Cloud Run        Workers

      Docker Host       Vertex AI        D1

       Raspberry Pi     Storage          KV

           │               │               │

           └───────────────┼───────────────┘

                    Unified Command Bus

Everything reports back to a single control plane.

AI Infrastructure Manager

Instead of manually creating infrastructure, the AI can recommend or automate changes based on user-defined policies.

Examples:

Local PC overloaded → suggest moving background workloads to Cloud Run.
Edge cache hit rate low → recommend deploying additional Cloudflare Workers and D1 replicas.
GitHub Actions queue building up → recommend self-hosted runners or alternative CI.
Storage nearing capacity → recommend archival or expansion.

Those changes should always be reviewable and, by default, require user approval before affecting live resources.

