One idea that fits your vision is to give every user an Infrastructure Genome: a versioned blueprint describing their entire environment.

It would include:

connected cloud providers
local machines
edge services
containers
databases
AI agents
permissions
network topology
deployment policies
automation rules

The simulation reads this genome to render the player's "world," while changes made through the platform update the genome. That gives users a portable, reproducible description of their environment that can evolve over time and be redeployed elsewhere if needed. It also keeps the simulation grounded in a real architecture rather than becoming just a visual game.

